#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0342 expect=skipped domain=ADAE
#note "structure=OCCDS is the DECLARED tier and beats the columns (Fix #154, corej.defineFirst=true), so the dataset's structure set is [OCCURRENCE DATA STRUCTURE], not in Scope.Data_Structures.Include -> out of scope, never runs -- even though the data (a 1-vs-1 tie) would fire if it ran. The batch's ONE pin on the [BASIC DATA STRUCTURE, MEDICAL DEVICE BASIC DATA STRUCTURE] Scope block, shared by AD0332/0333/0334/0342/0343/0403/0405. Worked precedent: pmda/PMDA-AD0142-skipped_occds_structure-ADAE.cdt."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
dataset ADAE structure=OCCDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col ANRLO   type=Num
col ANRLOC  type=Char
---
S1 | 001 | GLUC | 5.0 | 3 | LOWNORM
S1 | 002 | GLUC | 5.1 | 4 | LOWNORM
